    "description": "### Impact\r\n\r\nAn authenticated user can crash MariaDB versions 11.4 before 11.4.10 and 11.8 before 11.8.6 via a bug in  `JSON_SCHEMA_VALID()` function. Under certain conditions it might be possible to turn the crash into a remote code execution.\r\n\r\n### Patches\r\nThis issue is fixed in MariaDB 11.4.10, MariaDB 11.8.6, and MariaDB 12.2.2\r\n\r\n### References\r\nhttps://jira.mariadb.org/browse/MDEV-38356\r\n\r\n### Credits\r\nTeam [Xint Code](https://code.xint.io/) as part of [zeroday.cloud](https://zeroday.cloud)",
